# The context for docker/web.Dockerfile. BuildKit uses this file in place of the repository's root
# .dockerignore for that Dockerfile — which matters, because the root one excludes web/ (the .NET
# images need nothing from the Angular app) and would leave this build with an empty directory.
#
# Everything is excluded and the web app put back, so a new top-level directory is never uploaded
# by accident.
*

!web/
!docker/web/

# What a local `npm install`, `ng build` or test run leaves in web/, which is tens of thousands of
# files and would be copied over the container's own clean install.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.angular/
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
web/e2e/.auth/
